RESPONSIBILITIES
•             Assist Activity Supervisor to meal plan and prepare food as required; 
•             Handle, sort and serve meals, including breakfast, morning tea and lunch; 
•             Maintain kitchen area in a clean, safe and precise manner; sort and dispose of rubbish and organise laundering of kitchen linen; 
•             Clean food preparation equipment, floors, coffee machine, fridges, freezers and other kitchen tools and areas; 
•             Assist Activity Supervisor with ordering and receipting food and other supplies; 
•             Demonstrate a flexible and enthusiastic attitude towards undertaking a variety of tasks with a team approach; 
•             Actively participations in team meetings; 
•             Ensure all staff and job seekers are approached in a polite, courteous manner; 
•             Assist in the supervision of job seekers engaging in meaningful work like activities; 
•             Assist Activity Supervisor to ensure activities meet a high standard of workplace, health and safety standards; 
•             Assist with the completion of reports as required, such as weekly operational reports, job seeker photographs, and job seeker attendance records. 
•             Provide catering for staff on Friday to relieve activity supervisor to conduct other duties outside the kitchen space.
